# Anti-Patterns — What to NEVER Do

> This is the most important document for avoiding recurring mistakes.
> Every anti-pattern listed here is a REAL error that has actually been made.
> If you violate any rule in this document, STOP and fix it before continuing.

## TL;DR
- Circular buttons MUST be FIXED width = FIXED height with cornerRadius = size/2 — never HUG (AP-01, catastrophic)
- Only 1 primary CTA (filled) per screen; secondary actions use outlined or ghost style (AP-06)
- Use exactly 1 accent color for all primary actions; vary hierarchy by style (filled/outlined/ghost), not color (AP-02)
- Primary CTA always in the bottom half of the screen on mobile (thumb zone) (AP-07)
- Button labels must be verb + noun describing the action ("Send $150" not "OK" or "Submit") (AP-08)
- Show loading feedback within 100ms; display loading state if action takes > 400ms (AP-09)
- Consistent padding on all cards of the same type; follow the 8px grid (AP-03)
- Maximum 2 border-radius values + pill across the entire design (AP-04)
- Body text minimum 16px; font-weight 400+ for anything below 18px; maintain 4.5:1+ contrast ratio (AP-05)
- Modals must have at least 2 ways to close (X button + overlay tap or swipe) (AP-10)
- FILL sizing only works inside an auto-layout parent — set layoutMode FIRST (AP-12)
- Maximum 3-4 options for primary decisions (pricing, plans); provide a recommendation for larger sets (AP-26)
- Dark patterns are forbidden: no confirm-shaming, no hidden costs, no roach motels, no trick questions (AP-18 to AP-22)

