## ADDITIONS — Design Bible Architect Review

### DARK PATTERN ANTI-PATTERNS (Ethical Violations)

These are not just bad UX — they are ethically unacceptable. Never implement these:

#### AP-18: Confirm-Shaming
```
❌ WRONG:
"No thanks, I don't like saving money"  ← Manipulative dismiss text
"Yes, sign me up!"                      ← Positive option

✅ CORRECT:
"Subscribe to newsletter"               ← Clear action
"No thanks"                             ← Neutral, non-judgmental dismiss
```

#### AP-19: Roach Motel (Easy to Enter, Hard to Leave)
```
❌ WRONG:
Sign up: 1 click
Delete account: Settings > Account > Security > Advanced > Delete (5 levels deep)

✅ CORRECT:
Sign up: Simple flow
Delete account: Settings > Account > Delete Account (2 levels, clear path)
```

#### AP-20: Hidden Costs
```
❌ WRONG:
Product page shows "$29.99"
Checkout reveals "$29.99 + $8.99 shipping + $3.50 service fee + $2.00 tax"

✅ CORRECT:
Product page shows "$29.99 + shipping" with estimated total
Checkout shows itemized breakdown from the start
```

#### AP-21: Forced Continuity
```
❌ WRONG:
Free trial ends → Auto-charges with no warning

✅ CORRECT:
Free trial → Email 3 days before end → Clear cancellation option → Then charge
```

#### AP-22: Trick Questions
```
❌ WRONG:
□ Uncheck this box if you prefer not to not receive emails
  (Double negative, confusing)

✅ CORRECT:
□ Send me product updates via email
  (Clear, opt-in, honest)
```

### B2B/SAAS SPECIFIC ANTI-PATTERNS

#### AP-23: Feature Overload on First Use
```
❌ WRONG:
New user sees: Dashboard with 15 widgets, 12 sidebar items, 4 notifications,
tutorial overlay, upgrade banner, AND a survey popup

✅ CORRECT:
New user sees: Simplified dashboard with 3 key actions,
guided onboarding that reveals features progressively
```

#### AP-24: Settings Graveyard
```
❌ WRONG:
One massive settings page with 60+ options in no particular order

✅ CORRECT:
Settings organized by category (Account, Notifications, Integrations, Security)
Search within settings
Most common settings surfaced first
```

